Backend baseline:
  - internal/api/period_stats_handler.go — canonical handler for
    GET /api/v1/analytics/period-stats?vehicle_id=&days=
    Computes total_distance (km), total_drives, energy_used (kWh),
    avg_efficiency (Wh/km), total_cost (USD via base_cost_per_kwh),
    co2_saved (kg, distance_km * 0.120) over a trailing-day window.
    Reads SI canonical drives.distance_m / drives.duration_s and
    charging_sessions.total_energy_added_wh, converts to km/kWh at
    response boundary (Phase-42 rule).
    days <= 0 means "no date filter" (all-time) — respected by the
    parameterised SQL via NULL-checked WHERE clauses.

  - internal/api/router.go — chi mount of /analytics/period-stats
    + the existing /api/v1/ai/* mount block (mountAIRoutes).

  - internal/api/ai_routes.go — the canonical AI route mounter; one
    handler per feature, each wrapped in features.GuardedHandler so
