=== REASONING ===

Goal: layer an opt-in LLM narrator over the Period Compare page
without changing any deterministic calculation, while honouring
ADR-015 §I3 (baseline intact), §I5 (hidden UI in off mode), §I6
(404 routes in off mode), §I7 (per-feature toggle), §I10 (typed
DTOs through F4), and the methodology's P1-P10 + W1 wired-or-absent
contract.

Key design choices:

1. Shared compute helper, not duplicated SQL.
   Extracted ComputePeriodStats(ctx, db, vehicleID, days) into
   period_stats_handler.go. Both the canonical /analytics/period-stats
   handler AND the new AI tool adapter call this single function.
   No SQL is written twice. (Honesty pin matched against rubber-duck
   feedback on slice 0029.)

2. Strategy + Tool, not a one-shot handler.
   The narrator is implemented as a Strategy in
   internal/ai/strategies/period-compare-narration/ wired into the
   F4 dispatcher loop. The F4 tool query_period_compare is the
   only allowed tool — the LLM has no path to write or to call any
   other endpoint. The strategy is registered with the central
   feature registry; the SPA mirror is regenerated by aigen.

3. Read-only tool, propose-only contract.
   tools.PeriodCompare envelope carries vehicle_id, period_a,
   period_b (each with the six aggregate metrics), and a deltas
   array (one entry per metric, with nullable percent_change so a
   zero-baseline window does not divide-by-zero in the JSON). The
   tool's Mutates() returns false. Validation rejects vehicle_id
   <= 0, days outside [0, 3650], and unknown fields.

4. Presence-aware decode for "0 = all time".
   The SPA period selector accepts 0 = all-time; the backend treats
   days<=0 as "no date filter". A naive `if d == 0 { default }`
   on the handler-side parser would silently rewrite explicit
   all-time into the default 30. Solved by decoding the request
   body into map[string]json.RawMessage first, applying defaults
   only where keys are absent, then unmarshalling each present
   key. Manual unknown-field rejection covers the gap that
   DisallowUnknownFields leaves on the map path.

5. Decorator chain honoured.
   The strategy is wrapped via redactadapter.Wrap with the new
   PolicyPeriodCompareNarration (ClassVehicleName only). All
   provider calls flow through the standard redaction → rate-limit
   → cost-cap → audit → trace chain installed by the dispatcher
   factory.

6. SPA wired in this commit (P11/P12, W1 inline addendum).
   AIPeriodCompareNarration mirrors AICostForecastNarration:
   useAiStream is called unconditionally at the top of the body;
   the disabled prop is COMPUTED (`!canGenerate`); the body
   carries vehicle_id + days_a + days_b (0 forwarded as-is); the
   on-mode test asserts exactly one POST against
   /api/v1/ai/analytics/period-compare/narrate plus the
   double-submit guard plus the computed-disabled fallback when
   no vehicleId is in scope.

7. Off-mode invariant proven on both stacks.
   - Go: TestPeriodCompareNarrationAIOffShowsCardsOnly mounts the
     guarded route through routes.GuardedHandler with stub settings
     ai_mode='off' + per-feature toggle on, asserts HTTP 404.
   - React: same-named test asserts an empty container when
     ai_mode='off' even with the toggle on, an empty container
     when ai_mode='cloud' but the toggle is off, and the
     positive-control assertion that the gated wrapper renders
     when ai_mode='cloud' AND the toggle is on.

8. Goldens pass through the F6 mock provider.
   3 deterministic goldens cover (a) typical period comparison
   with positive deltas, (b) zero-data Period A (proves
   nullable percent_change + zero-baseline honesty),
   (c) refusal of an out-of-scope vehicle. Each golden has a
   matching canned/*.yaml that the F6 mock provider replays;
   rubric judge_pass_threshold=4.

